---
import { modules } from '../data/modules';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';

const built = modules.filter((m) => m.status === 'built').length;

// Category-level comparison only. No prices or feature counts for named products,
// because those change and we would rather be vague than wrong.
const cols = ['ShipStack', 'Paid starter kits', 'Hosted services'];
const rows: { k: string; v: [string, string, string]; win?: 0 | 1 | 2 }[] = [
  {
    k: 'License',
    v: ['MIT', 'Commercial license per buyer', 'Proprietary service (some are open source and self-hostable)'],
  },
  {
    k: 'Hosting',
    v: ['None. Libraries that run inside your app; there is no ShipStack service.', 'Your app, on your hosting', 'They run it for you'],
  },
  {
    k: 'Cost',
    v: ['Free. You run the infrastructure.', 'One-time purchase', 'Subscription or usage-based, usually with a free tier'],
  },
  {
    k: 'Lock-in',
    v: ['Per part, at the adapter. Remove one part, keep the rest.', 'You own the copied code, but it is shaped around the kit\'s stack.', 'Their API, SDK and data model'],
    win: 0,
  },
  {
    k: 'Your data',
    v: ['In your database, in tables you can read', 'In your database', 'On the vendor\'s servers; export varies'],
  },
  {
    k: 'Scope today',
    v: [
      built === modules.length
        ? `${modules.length} small backend parts at v0.1. No UI. Auth is email and password only: no OAuth, passkeys, MFA or organizations.`
        : `${modules.length} parts planned, ${built} built. Backend only, no UI.`,
      'A whole app on day one: UI, auth, billing, landing page',
      'Deep and polished in one domain: social login, SSO, dashboards, support',
    ],
    win: 1,
  },
  {
    k: 'Maturity',
    v: ['v0.x, no independent security audit yet', 'Varies by kit', 'Mature products with dedicated teams'],
    win: 2,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="compare" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead no="05" kicker="Honest comparison" title="Where we win, and where we clearly don't." id="compare-title">
      We lose on breadth and maturity, by a lot. Auth is deliberately small and is not a Clerk or Better Auth replacement.
      If you want a complete app today, buy a starter kit. If you want SSO, dashboards and someone else on call, use a
      hosted service such as Clerk, Knock or Trigger.dev. ShipStack is for the code you would rather own.
    </SectionHead>

    <div class="cmp">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">ShipStack compared with paid starter kits and hosted services</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            {cols.map((c, i) => <th scope="col" class:list={{ us: i === 0 }}>{c}</th>)}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.k}</th>
                {r.v.map((v, i) => (
                  <td class:list={{ us: i === 0, win: r.win === i }} data-col={cols[i]}>
                    {r.win === i && <span class="win__mark">Better here</span>}
                    {v}
                  </td>
                ))}
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cmp {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    table-layout: fixed;
  }
  thead th {
    padding: var(--s2);
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  tbody th {
    width: 160px;
    padding: var(--s2) var(--s2) var(--s2) 0;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  thead td {
    width: 160px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  tbody td {
    padding: var(--s2);
    vertical-align: top;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .us {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    color: var(--ink);
    box-shadow:
      inset 2px 0 0 var(--ink),
      inset -2px 0 0 var(--ink);
  }
  thead th.us {
    box-shadow:
      inset 2px 0 0 var(--ink),
      inset -2px 0 0 var(--ink),
      inset 0 6px 0 var(--signal);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child .us {
    box-shadow:
      inset 2px 0 0 var(--ink),
      inset -2px 0 0 var(--ink),
      inset 0 -2px 0 var(--ink);
  }
  .win {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* Small screens: one block per criterion, the three answers stacked and labelled. */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .cmp {
      overflow: visible;
    }
    table,
    tbody,
    tr,
    th,
    td {
      display: block;
      width: auto;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    thead {
      display: none;
    }
    tbody tr {
      padding: var(--s2) 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    }
    tbody th {
      padding: 0 0 var(--s1);
      border: 0;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    tbody td {
      padding: 10px 12px;
      border: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    tbody td::before {
      content: attr(data-col);
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 2px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.6875rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-3);
    }
    .us,
    tbody tr:last-child .us {
      box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--signal);
    }
  }
  .win__mark {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }
</style>
